' Question: what runs on which thread when the owner saves a webhook or sends a test from Tools > Options > Alerts?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md. Drawn by hand; the steps are cited there and in ../05-building-blocks.md.
@startuml 06-options-save-and-test
participant "Alerts page\n(UI thread)" as P
participant "Pool thread" as W
participant DiscordWebhookSetup as S
participant "ISecretStore\n(keyring)" as K
participant SendTestToConfiguredChannels as T
participant DescriptorChannelCatalogBuilder as B
participant DiscordWebhookChannel as D
participant Discord as X

== Save ==
P -> P : begin action n (ActionOwnershipTracker),\nbuttons off, "Saving the webhook..."
P -> W : submit(save(text))
W -> S : save(text)
S -> S : strip, is_discord_webhook_url?\nno: REFUSED, nothing written
S -> K : write("alerting_discord_webhook", url)
S -> K : read(...) must equal url, else OVERRIDDEN
W --> P : relay: (n, SAVE, WebhookSave)
P -> P : still action n? then clear the field,\nshow the sentence and the 4-character hint

== Send test ==
P -> W : submit(run())
W -> T : run()
T -> B : build()
B -> K : read(...) via discord_channel(): no webhook, no channel
T -> D : deliver(TEST alert, LOUD)
D -> X : POST
X --> D : 404
D --> T : refused("Discord refused the webhook message (404)")
W --> P : relay: (n, TEST, outcomes)
P -> P : still action n? then show the sanitised reason
note over P, W : the URL crosses only P -> S and S -> K -> D -> X;\nan exception from the worker is shown by its type name alone
@enduml
